:: Display Settings [widget]
<<widget "npcsettings">>
	<div class="settingsGrid">
		<div class="settingsHeader options">NPC Display</div>
			<div class="settingsToggleItemWide">
				<span class="green">NPC Display will display an image of a named NPC if they are present in the scene. To add an NPC image, go into the npc folder in the img folder and replace the character you want to use.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="gold">NPC Display:</span><br>
				<label>Enabled <<radiovar "$NPCenable" "1">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>Disabled <<radiovar "$NPCenable" "0">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label>
			</div>
			<div class="settingsToggleItemWide">
				<span class="green">The creator pack will change all NNPC sprites to the ones created by the chosen user.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="gold">Creator Pack:</span><br>
				<label>mozumelody <<radiovar "$creatorname" "mozumelody">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>CDNPC
				<mouse class = "tooltip linkBlue">(?)
				        <span>
				            Use the Custom Dynamic NPC Portraits Mod in the sidebar
                        </span>
                </mouse>
                <<radiovar "$creatorname" "cdnpc">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>Custom <<radiovar "$creatorname" "custom">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label>
			</div>
			<div class="settingsToggleItemWide">
				<span class="green">Static NPC display will display the NPC's named files, found in the npc folder inside the img folder.<br><br>
				Dynamic NPCs will automatically adjust for NPC sex, skin color, and species in the cases of Great Hawk and Black Wolf.<br><br>
				These dynamic files can be found inside the npc folder, go into the folders labeled with each NPC name, the sex of the NPC, m for male, f for female, then the skin color black, white, or monster.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="gold">NPC Display Type:</span><br>
				<label>Dynamic <<radiovar "$NPCstatic" "0">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>Static <<radiovar "$NPCstatic" "1">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label>
			</div>
			<div class="settingsToggleItemWide">
				<span class="green">The layering of the NPC. Behind will display the NPC behind the player, in front will display them in front.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="gold">NPC Display Position:</span><br>
				<label>Behind <<radiovar "$NPCposition" "1">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>In Front <<radiovar "$NPCposition" "2">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label>
			</div>
	</div>
<</widget>>
<<widget "backgrounds">>
	<div class="settingsGrid">
		<div class="settingsHeader options">Backgrounds</div>
			<div class="settingsToggleItemWide">
				<span class="green">Dynamic images will change to reflect the current location. These can be replaced in the backgrounds folder, found in the img folder, by replacing the location image with a new one. Make sure to keep the name the same.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="gold">Background Type:</span><br>
				<label>Dynamic <<radiovar "$staticimages" "0">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>Static <<radiovar "$staticimages" "1">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
				<label>Disabled <<radiovar "$staticimages" "2">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> 
				<br><br>
				<span class="green">Static background images are images that will be displayed at all times when selected. Just enter the static image folder inside backgrounds and replace the number you want to use.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="red">Backgrounds over 100 are not supported and will result in an error if the files are not self inserted.</span>
				<br><br>
				<span class="gold">Static Background Options:</span><br>
					<label>Background 1 <<radiovar "$static" "1">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
					<label>Background 2 <<radiovar "$static" "2">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
					<label>Background 3 <<radiovar "$static" "3">><<updatesidebarimg>><</radiovar>></label> |
